
(iii)Give the details of the authors who have 2 or more books in the catalog and the price of the books is greater than the average price of the books in the catalog and the year of publication after 2010.
SELECT A.AUTHOR_ID, A.NAME, COUNT(C.BOOK_ID) AS NO_OF_BOOKS
FROM AUTHOR A
JOIN CATLOG C ON A.AUTHOR_ID = C.AUTHOR_ID
WHERE C.PRICE > (SELECT AVG(PRICE) FROM CATLOG)
AND C.YEAR > 2010
GROUP BY A.AUTHOR_ID, A.NAME
HAVING COUNT(C.BOOK_ID) >= 2;


iv) Find the author of the book that has maximum sales.

SELECT A.NAME, C.TITLE, O.QUANTITY
FROM ORDER_DETAILS O
JOIN CATLOG C ON O.BOOK_ID = C.BOOK_ID
JOIN AUTHOR A ON C.AUTHOR_ID = A.AUTHOR_ID
WHERE O.QUANTITY = (SELECT MAX(QUANTITY) FROM ORDER_DETAILS);



(v) Demonstrate how to increase the price of the books published by the specific publisher by 10%
UPDATE CATLOG
SET PRICE = PRICE * 1.10
WHERE PUBLISHER_ID = 1;


